<br>
If your years of solitude have taught you anything, it is that one can sustain her soul on dewdrops and dawnlight alone, and worldly concerns should only matter insofar as the body is still capable of work.
<br>
It has also taught you that the mind can be quite asleep, even if the eyes are open, and time, unbounded by attention, rushes on and on like a flood.

