Taking a wide berth from the pavilion, you make it down the gravel slope towards the shore, where a Bureau boat is beached. For a moment, you imagine (link-reveal: "commandeering the craft")[, but you quickly remember that you don’t know how to start the thing up, much less pilot it.
<br>
So, you (link-reveal: "pace into the reed thickets")[, (if: $lockPanicYou is true)[holding the canvas over your head so that it won’t get wet, ]sinking your ankles into the mud, intent on trekking through the woods (link-reveal: "and…")[
<br>
//“We’ve got one over here!”// A woman’s voice echoes in the trees, startling you. Flashlights reach into the reeds, touching you.
