:: Ants B {"position":"5825,1975","size":"100,100"}
{=

(set: $activity to "a surprise offensive")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

<!--Ants' second attack-->
(set: $lockAntsB to true)

Night has not entirely left, and still, you've already arrived in the waking world. (link-reveal: "Why?")[
<br>
//"Mraow?! Mraow?!"//
<br>
Jesse has been meowing and rubbing onto you. Groggily, you reach out to stroke her, but she twists away and continues her cries.
<br>
(link-reveal: "What's wrong with her?")[ You hear her in the dark, contorting and wrestling with herself, repeatedly kicking at her own face, then slamming her head down onto the floor. Pain radiates through your skin as though the torment is your own. (if: $lockJesseE1 is true)[Does she hate her cone that much?]
<br>
You rush to her side. You can't see clearly, can't make out her face, not with this busy static infecting all that is dark, and everything is dark at this hour. You try to hold her tight and stroke between those fearful eyes. Jesse screams. To your surprise, the static which coats her face clears away where you touch, and it has a (link-reveal: "tangible texture.")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "Hard")[, like tiny sand grains.
<br>
(link-reveal: "Moist")[, when you rub your fingers together.
<br>
(link-reveal: "Wiggling")[, living.
<br>
(link-reveal: "Hot")[, so hot it stings, and by unison, your entire body comes afire.
<br>
You yelp and jolt back, and black masses shed from Jesse's fur, shattering onto the floor into a million grains, each crawling back into the cracks in the floorboard. Jesse wrings herself out of your arms and flees atop the wardrobe, where she continues to kick the things off of her, raining hateful specks down on you.
<br>
The ants - (link-reveal: "they're everywhere.")[ They've built hives under your blanket. They've formed dark, pulsing tendrils on the wall. They're in your clothes, mindlessly biting.
<br>
//"Mroow? Mroooow?"// Jesse asks no-one but the void, as if saying, //"Why? Why me?"//
<br>

(link: "Kill them.")[(dialog: [They die.], "More comes.")(link: "Kill them, again!")[(dialog: [More of them die.], "Yet more comes.")(link: "Again!")[(dialog: [They die without knowing what kills them.], "And more comes without knowing why.")(link: "Again!")[(show: ?hidden)]
]]]

[
<br>
(link-reveal: "An hour has passed.")[ (link-reveal: "Daylight is now in full bloom.")[
<br>
You don't remember what you've been doing, but there is blood under your fingernails, and your skin - oh, if only you could shed it like clothes and burn it, you would, if only to stop this itch.
<br>
Wet tissue papers pile up in the bin, each capturing about a hundred dead ants. Yet, the room is still crawling with static, always on your vision's peripheries. Are there still more of them, or is it your own paranoia? (if: $storyAnts's qt is 2)[Paranoia is not paranoia if it is plausible; you thought you've cleaned up the place, but evidently not enough.]
<br>
(link-reveal: "The walls")[ are made of ants; (link-reveal: "the plaster")[ is full of ants; (link-reveal: "the mortar")[ comes pre-mixed with ant eggs; (link-reveal: "the floorboard")[ hides colonies after colonies; (link-reveal: "your own flesh")[ houses who knows how many larvaes, each pore violated while you sleep.
<br>
(link-reveal: "You consider kerosene and flame")[ but think better of it. (link-reveal: "You consider the knife")[ but think better of it. (link-reveal: "You consider")[-
<br>
//"Miu…"// Jesse calls out weakly from her hiding place.
<br>
(link-reveal: "They've hurt Jesse.")[ No, there has to be a subtler, more efficient, //crueler// way to go about this. Run your blood cold, or else they will sense your presence and see you coming. There is nothing left to do but act.
<br>
---
(link: "Kill them all.")[
(set: $storyAnts's qt to 3)
(dialog: [(print: $storyAnts's name) resumes.
<br>It has come to your attention that the six-legged menace is still at large. You will have to extinguish that problem promptly, or Jesse's torment, and by extension yours, will be unending.], "Grit your teeth and act.")
	(print: $actionDamage's effect)
	(print: $actionBack's effect)
] <span class="desc">(Your mind falters slightly. You return to your morning with greater urgency.)</span>

]
]]]
]]]]]
