:: Ants C4 {"position":"5550,1800","size":"100,100"}
{=

(set: $activity to "laying down")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

That night, as you turn off the lights, the last thing you see are dark tendrils slithering from nooks and cracks you didn't know existed, wrapping themselves around those honey-pearls you've laid around the apartment. Tentacles to the stars. You tell Jesse good night. (link-reveal: "The light goes out.")[
<br>
You sleep, heavy with hope, caught somewhere in your throat, urging your heart to squeeze. It's always darkest before dawn. And dawn will come. But now, in the pitch-black apartment, a shadow falls over you. (link-reveal: "A man.")[
(set: $activity to "a dream of a man")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]
<br>
You stare with blinded eyes at his fuzzy form. You open your mouth to (link-reveal: "ask who he is.")[ No sound comes. He doesn't speak either. You can't even hear him breathe.
<br>
(link-reveal: "You try to move")[, but there is only a ghostly impression of movement. Your body is right where it was - under his flickering shadow. (link-reveal: "His turn.")[
<br>
He reaches out, or rather falls onto your mattress. The mattress does not depress; he is weightless, like a veil of rain falling onto a mountain, like hairs on your feet, hairs of fire, burning wherever they touch. Tears run down your face, and the stinging crawls up your shins, your knees, your thighs and the shadow is lowering himself onto you. Next - your face, to be burned to the bones with a kiss.
<br>
(link-reveal: "You try to scream.")[ A cough comes out. The man is closer now; a million tiny eyes gaze at you with stupefying hunger; a million jaws snap at the pale, fearful Sun. (link-reveal: "You try to scream again.")[ A hiss, not from your own throat but from another corner of the room, reverberates.
<br>
(link-reveal: "//\"Mmmraoooww!!!\"//")[
<br>
Jesse shrieks her warcry and launches herself in the air. Her body is a wrecking ball, shattering the shadow's head into chunks, which crumble onto the side of the mattress, by the side of your pillow, barely missing your gaping mouth. As each piece meets solid ground, it disintegrates into all the weak, cowardly, and selfish individuals that made up what momentarily have seemed like true terror.
<br>
Finally able to move at last, you desperately wipe away and spit out the ants that have lost their ways and are trying to flee into your mouth.
<br>
Before you, Jesse continues her battle with the headless assailant. It swallows her into itself. She breaks out again, screaming, and the shadow flails its terrible appendages against her tiny body with a (link-reveal: "\"thud, thud, thud\".")[
<br>
Despite your horror and disgust, you (link-reveal: "join in the fray.")[ Each kick feels as though your shin has hit the hard bark of a very soft oak. It spills more of itself onto the floor until the shadow is wholly dissolved into a wiggling puddle. The broken deserters scramble to steal their own pieces of the honeyed Sun, this fight having been lost. You chase them down and (link-reveal: "stomp")[ and (link-reveal: "stomp")[ and (link-reveal: "stomp")[ until you can no longer feel the soles of your feet.
<br>
Now, you are kneeling on the floor, curling over, throwing up. Your vision throbs with (link-reveal: "a strange and vital light.")[
<br>
But before you can see what it is…
<br>
---
(link: "You pass out from exhaustion.")[
	(set: $lockAntsC4 to true)
	(set: $mind to 1)
	(dialog: [As you fade out, you hear Jesse's wheezing synchronizing with yours. Your last thought is that Jesse is not well. She needs you.
<br><span class="desc">Your mind is significantly damaged by this experience.</span>], "You must live!")
	(goto: "DeathCheck")
]
]]]]]]]]]]]]]]<!--passage's end-->


