:: Ants C5b {"position":"6200,2250","size":"100,100"}
{=

<!--Amy's route-->

(set: $time to "Midday")(replace: ?time)[$time]
(set: $activity to "on the phone with Amy")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

//"Oh… oh yeah, no problem. I'd love to. Yeah,"// Amy says, (link-reveal: "voice tired.")[ She was slow to pick up the phone, as if unsure whether she should do so at all. //"Jesse can even stay with me at my dorm. I get lonely over the summer."//
<br>
Oh? Doesn't she plan to go back home to her mom? Silence, then (link-reveal: "an answer,")[
<br>
//"... No, who's going to do coffee runs and fetch photocopies at Montlake? With the staff shortage, maybe an intern like me will have a chance at something more important, haha."//
<br>
That's right. So unfair. If they make us crawl, we'll have to eat anything that falls on the floor, right? No blame there.
<br>
//"Mom's been busy anyway. Won't even text back. We'll just end up arguing if I'm there."//
<br>
Speaking of, how's (link-reveal: "that thing with her aunt?")[(show:?hidden1)] - You force yourself to sound concerned.

[
<br>
//"Erm… So, how are we doing this? With Jesse, I mean,"// Amy changes the subject, much to your relief.
<br>
After (link-reveal: "going back and forth over schedules")[ - Amy won't have time to make frequent trips to your apartment like before - you settle on leaving the apartment key under your front carpet, with everything ready-packed for Jesse. Amy will (link-reveal: "drop by after you're gone.")[
<br>
//"Hey, sorry that I won't be able to see you off. And sorry that, well… Nevermind. Congrats on that gala thing, by the way. I don't think you've told me."//
<br>
Yes, it's (link-reveal: "all very short-notice.")[ It's no big deal; you didn't even think that it was worth mentioning. You'll only be gone for like two or three days. Four, tops. The lakes are lovely this time of the year, and you wish you could take her with you.
<br>
//"Yeah, I didn't think this type of stuff was still going on. I guess life moves on, right?"//
<br>
(link-reveal: "Right.")[
<br>
//"Well, I'll be there the day after. Tell Jesse I said 'hi', OK? Hope she doesn't mind Auntie Amy's cramped dorm room."//
<br>
Very good. Amy hangs up before you could bring up something else. It doesn't matter. As long as she still answers your call, as long as there's still an excuse to see her again…
<br>
The Sun is lowering again. You look around the apartment and see nothing moving. (link-reveal: "No sign of life.")[
<br>
---
