:: Ants C5d {"position":"6200,2450","size":"100,100"}
<!--Lonely route-->

(set: $time to "Midday")(replace: ?time)[$time]
(set: $activity to "leaving the window open")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

You've learned online that cats must eat nearly everyday, otherwise, they will start developing serious health problems. Leaving a lot of kibbles out before you leave might be an option, although your recent experience with open foodstuff in the apartment has taught you that this isn't without its issues.
<br>
Then… (link-reveal: "there's always the window.")[

(set: _num to 0)
(set: _trigger to "(set: _num to it +1)(if: _num >= 2)[(show: ?whatChoice)]")

<br>
(link-reveal: "How can you even think about it?")[ Your apartment has one large window, leading out to a single "balcony", although the pipes and air conditioning units have made that space unusable as such. This window has been permanently shut ever since you adopted Jesse. You've heard of many stories of cats falling to their deaths, and you live high up enough for the fall to maim, if not to kill. Jesse is your responsibility; and it is your responsibility to keep that window shut._trigger ]
<br>
(link-reveal: "Why are you thinking about it?")[ Face it: Jesse stands a better chance of surviving out there, even if she has to hunt for herself, than she does locked in here, with a supply of food that might very well become inedible the moment you turn your eyes away. The ants - you've killed all of them, right? You can't be too sure. You can't, not when Jesse's wellbeing is on the line._trigger ]

[
<br>
(link-reveal: "What choice do you have? You've done everything right.")[ Yes, you have. You've done your best, and your best still isn't enough because your best is //yours//. It has always revolved around what //you// wanted out of Jesse, not what //she// needed. Otherwise, you would've taken better care of her living space. You would've taken her to the vet every other month for checkups. You would've given her better food and played with her more. You would've taken her out on walks at the park, where she might have chased butterflies and meowed at other cats. She might have had a far happier, more fulfilling life, if fate didn't put you into her way. But fate didn't have anything to do with it; it was all your fault. You decided, everyday, that this was acceptable to her - locked up in here, half-rotting with a half-corpse, eating where she shat, bored out of her mind, only to be…
<br>
(link-reveal: "But there is always the window.")[ You've already failed, but you can always do what is right. You can truly leave it up to fate, blameless fate. Not everything has to go the way you want. You are not the sole arbiter of goodness. Even a cat has its own will, too.
<br>
Wipe away the tears. (link-reveal: "Open the window now")[, even if you do not plan to leave today, even if the ants never return. Let her go as she pleases. If she loves you, she'll return. If she doesn't, then you'll mourn. At least she has an option.
<br>
(link-reveal: "So you do.")[ The thick, smoky air crawls inside and seeps into your lungs, and all the unpleasant smells inside the apartment stop mattering so much.
<br>
With a trembling voice, you call out to Jesse, telling her that if the ants reappear while you're gone, she should not worry for you and instead save herself first. Because, if anything happens to her, you won't be able to bear it. No more heroics, OK?
<br>
Silence. (link-reveal: "All the ants are dead.")[(show: ?done)] Did you really need to do this?
[
<br>
---
(link: "This fight is well and truly over.")[
	(set: $choiceJesseGala to "window")
    (print: $storyAnts's gainEffect)
    (dialog: [Thanks to your bait, the ants are all gone.], "Gone, gone, never to return.")
    (print: $attProgress's gainEffect)
    (print: $actionOnward's effect)
    ] <span class="desc">(Complete ''(print: $storyAnts's name)'' and be ''satisfied''. Move on with your life.)</span>
]<done|(hide:?done)
]]]]]<whatChoice|(hide:?whatChoice)
]


:: Ants C5 (healthy) {"position":"5825,2225","size":"100,100"}
{=
(set: $activity to "a reprieve")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

<!--Next morning, finding out the Jesse's healing-->

For days now, maybe weeks, a drowsy smog has choked the air. But this morning, there is a (link-reveal: "brief moment of mercy")[, and a ray of light shines through a crack in the sky and warms the spot where Jesse is resting.
<br>
(link-reveal: "She blinks slowly at you")[, then nods off, breathing steadily. You pet her. She twitches but does not move. It's strange. She never sleeps during the day. Something - distant and half-remembered - tells you that she now needs all the rest she can have. The cone she wears glows with a prideful halo in the morning light.
<br>
Looking around, you see (link-reveal: "a battlefield.")[ Ant corpses are piling up in dark, reddish clumps all over the apartment. But they don't seem to have increased since yesterday. Perhaps all the ants are finally gone. A million lives have been snuffed out. (link-reveal: "You have your peace now.")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "But at what cost?")[ You check Jesse again for fresh wounds. There are those that have newly appeared; each of them sends a pain on your own face, radiating down your spine, as though they are your own wounds. But the old ones have turned a dry orange-yellow around dark scabs. They're healing. Jesse is healing. (link-reveal: "The medicine is working.")[
<br>
She purrs when you pet her, and you begin to wonder - (link-reveal: "was any of this necessary?")[ All this suffering would have been avoided if you had been more careful, more diligent with how you live. Live small and quietly, clean up after yourself, leave little trace. Neither you nor the ants would have known of each other's existence. And, above all else, Jesse wouldn't be in this miserable state. Perhaps, (link-reveal: "if she has never met you…")[
<br>
Ah, none of these thoughts are new. Sometimes, battering yourself with what-ifs is only a way to defer action. This time, (link-reveal: "you've acted.")[ The questions disappear; the Gordian knot has been slashed decisively. So long as you act, that you will your thoughts into reality, the heavy clouds of consideration will lift. Not always, but this time, it mattered.
<br>
Then (link-reveal: "why did you put off painting for years?")[ What if you had started earlier, would you be readier for the Gala? What if you strove for less, moved more quietly, and tended only to your own garden? What if you worked harder and ignored everything else? What if you were more earnest with you-know-who? What if you had left (cycling-link: "Katherine", "Simone", "Specht", "Becca", "Jenny", "Philo", "Erik", "Annie", "the church sister Winnipeg", "the rest of them") well enough alone? These questions, too, (link-reveal: "disappear.")[
<br>

(if: $eventShow's timer >= 0)[That's right, you're going places. Places with many more names. You need to get your business in order, so you can lift your wings. And, while you're gone, (link-reveal: "who will look after Jesse?")[(show: ?choices)]]

(else:)[
What use is there to think of any other life but this one? A million had perished last night. And here you are. Thus, for this life…
<br>
---
(link: "... There is nothing to do but paint.")[
