(set: $activity to "police cars in the streets")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

<!--Already missed Gala, midday police across the street-->

(set: $lockPoliceB to true)

The day is dark and fog-choked. The brightest lights now are (link-reveal: "stark red and blue")[, flashing through your windows. On the other side of the street, the police van has left its over-head on for a while, as though without a beacon, the officers won't find their way back from whichever house they're raiding.
<br>
(link-reveal: "But what are they raiding for?")[ Since Mrs. Wong's disappearance, they haven't come back to ask anyone anything. Maybe it's already a lost cause. Maybe they've lost their way in the (link-reveal: "fog.")[
<br>
Now, they're (link-reveal: "bringing out a woman")[ - or rather, wheeling her out on a cargo trolley]. Her hands are held high up in the air, frozen. The confused family tries to explain (link-rerun: "something")[(dialog: [Something like, //"We don't know where she came from."// Or, //"We didn't do it; she was like that when we found her."// It's all they can do.], "It's all they know.")] to an officer, but he only nods. His colleagues load the stiff woman into their van, and they drive off. The children are hushed back inside (link-rerun: "the house")[(dialog: [House after house after house. It's getting more common. Or maybe it's always been this way. You wouldn't know.], "You try not to think about it.")]. No-one is left in the streets. No-one but (link-reveal: "a black car.")[
<br>

(set: _num to 0)
