:: Jesse-Amy A1 {"position":"5000,4025","size":"100,100"}
{=

(set: $activity to "staying very still in the dark")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

The latch clicks, and (link-reveal: "the front door opens.")[
<br>
//"Shit, shit, shit,"// you hear a girl's voice - nasally, as though (link-reveal: "she's been crying.")[ //"Jesse? Are you there, little baby? Fuck, I'm so sorry that I'm late. I'm so sorry."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "It's Amy.")[ (cycling-link: "You've forgotten all about her.", "You've let yourself forget.", "You've not let yourself hope.(show:?hidden1)",)` `[But she's here. She thinks you're at the Greeting Gala. You should go out there and tell her that you've called it off, that she should go away, that she shouldn't involve herself with you anymore.

[
<br>
---
]<del|
(link: "It's the right thing to do.")[
(hide:?del)
<br>
And yet, your body won't move. It clings onto this last tether of hope. (link-reveal: "Amy.")[ The gala might be over, but greatness is still here, blindly stumbling in your living room, searching for the light. Let her have an excuse to (link-reveal: "come back")[, to (link-reveal: "sit there in the Sun for you")[, and you will slowly (link-reveal: "lift her veil…")[
<br>
//"Jesse? Tsk. You haven't even finished your bowl… Ugh, it stinks."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "The phone rings.")[ Your heart jumps. Thank heavens, (link-reveal: "it's not yours.")[
<br>
//"Hello? Have you gotten a hold of her yet? ... No, why do I have to talk to- OK, give it to them… Yes, this is Mrs. Wong's daughter… No, I haven't been able to contact her since last week or so… No, I'm not in town; I'm in Seattle… For college, yes… Yes, that's her sister… No, she hasn't 'appeared'. But why did you say it like that? Auntie's not… No, I understand… I understand… No, my father's passed away… Uh-huh… Uh-huh…"//
<br>
(link-reveal: "She goes on like that for a while")[, shuffling around the apartment, sniffling all the while. Then, a clatter and a curse. She must have tossed her phone on the table. (link-reveal: "There was no goodbye.")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "//\"God,\"//")[ Amy whispers. //"Show me a way out. And give me the strength to walk it."//
<br>
Then comes a silence so long and utter that she might hear you breathe. So, you (link-reveal: "stop breathing.")[
<br>
From the footsteps on the floorboard, you can tell that she is (link-reveal: "slowly approaching your painting.")[ She once asked to see it, but you didn't let her. Creak - she is (link-reveal: "kneeling down.")[ Rustling - she is (link-reveal: "pulling apart the linen curtain that hangs over the painting.")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "Amy gasps.")[ And with this one breath, a droning music blows in like gusts from unseen lands. The crack under the bathroom door begins to shimmer with a strange, oily light, as though the painting itself is (link-reveal: "flowing into the world.")[
	(if: $storyAnts's healthy is true)[(show: ?alive)]
	(else:)[(show: ?dead)]
]
]]]]]]]]]]]]]]] [<span class="desc">(Commit.)</span>]<del|

