:: Jesse-Henri A {"position":"5150,3900","size":"100,100"}
{=
(set: $place to "at Henri's place")(replace: ?place)[$place]
(set: $activity to "picking up Jesse")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

(set: $lockJesseHenriA to true)

(link-reveal: "It's been long enough.")[ Enough for Henri to think that you've made a very important trip and have just come back. In truth, you've been hiding in your apartment, sustaining on leftovers in the fridge. Time to stop being a rat and be human again, if only for a little while. Jesse is waiting for you. Poor baby, she must miss you a great deal.
<br>
You change into an outfit - something to suggest that you've just come out of an important event, boarded the bus, and came straight home. Then, you (link-reveal: "head down the hall")[, towards Henri's unit. Behind the door, there is droning music, like the TV's left on. You (link-reveal: "knock.")[
<br>
//"W- who is that?"// You hear Henri's voice, sounding somewhat cautious.
<br>
You say that (link-reveal: "it's just you.")[ Again. Like always. The door (link-reveal: "cracks open")[, its chain still latched.
<br>
//"Ah… if it isn't the world-famous painter! Am I glad to see you!"// Henri says as he peeks out. His eyes are bloodshot. Stray hair drapes over his familiar smile. //"Lemme get the lock for you… Yep, here we go… Come on, quickly!"//
<br>
The moment you step into the (link-rerun: "strangely dark apartment")[(dialog: [All the blinds are shut, and all the lights are off, save for the glow from his computer. Or rather, //computers//.], "If they could be called that.")], he closes and (link-reveal: "locks the door behind you.")[
<br>
//"Here, be careful not to trip. Oh the guys at the lab are going to kill me if they see this cable management. So, tea, as usual?"//
<br>
(link-reveal: "You nod")[ just so he would leave you alone for a second. It's only been a minute, and you're already suffocating. Perhaps you've been spoiled by the past few days of being alone. The air smells of burnt ozone, like how you'd imagine lightning to smell. And there's a different, fainter //stink// too. Familiar. Reminds you of your own apartment before you cleaned it up.
<br>
As Henri performs some light acrobatics over his beeping, whirling mess, through which is the kitchen counter, also filled with boxes, you take a moment to (link-reveal: "observe the apartment.")[ The scene reminds you of the electronic waste mountains in Ghana. Only, some particularly diligent and fixated magpie has built a breathing, blinking, groaning nest out of such waste. "Fixated" seems to be the operant word here. Some people bring their work home; Henri brings an entire infrastructure. Did he say something about (link-reveal: "a //hobby//?")[
<br>
(link: "But then, his voice interrupts your thoughts.")[//"So? How did it go?"// He calls out from the obscured kitchen. (link-reveal: "//\"The show, I mean.\"//")[(show:?choices1)]
]]]]]]]]]]

[<ul>
<li>(link: "It was everything you imagined it to be.")[(hide:?choices1)(replace:?show)[
<br>You tell him that the Greeting Gala was everything you'd imagined it to be. That is to say, nothing, because you didn't go, and you haven't even thought about what it would be like either. Nothing about it was normal. You were given a terribly short deadline. Your painting wasn't ready. (link-reveal: "You weren't ready.")[
<br>(link-reveal: "But you tell him none of this.")[ Instead, you pulled from whatever you could remember of other Darkbloom-funded shows in the past, even sprinkling in some salacious details - this touchy-feely senator, that Texas-aligned heiress, those addled starlets, in various combinations or all together. But, Henri doesn't seem all that interested in these… human melodramas. He's only interested in how your new works were received, but you (link-reveal: "pretend not to hear him.")[(show:?hidden1)]]]]]

<li>(link: "It was a terrible bore.")[(hide:?choices1)(replace:?show)[
<br>You tell him that the Greeting Gala was a terrible bore. It seemed as though the rich did everything to copy what they saw in the media about how an elite life ought to be. But the media is copying the rich. (link-reveal: "Who's copying whom?")[
<br>This incestuous memetic recycling amplifies only the loudest, most irritating most, //gilded// elements, so that everything becomes a satire of itself and itself only, completely detached from anything real.
<br>//"Oh yes, in my field of work, we call that a 'model collapse'."//
<br>You give him a half-hearted (link-reveal: "uh-huh.")[ Words, words, words; they're just words. Even these acidic words of yours are a copy of what you think a sharp-witted critic ought to sound like. Since, you know, you (link-reveal: "didn't actually go.")[(show:?hidden1)]]]]]

<li>(link: "You're still processing.")[(hide:?choices1)(replace:?show)[
<br>You tell him that you're still digesting what went down. Sometimes, (link-reveal: "a void is the hardest to swallow.")[
<br>//"Heh, you're just being humble,"// Henri says as he turns off the boiler. //"Those people are lucky to have been there. I'm sure your works wowed them, just as they've wowed me before."//
<br>Yes, (link-reveal: "perhaps he would be right")[, if his artistic opinion was of any weight. But no, Henri has always been breathlessly supportive, and maybe that's a good quality in a husband - you'll leave that for other women to find out - but it makes for a poor critic.
<br>But what need is there for a critic? (link-reveal: "You already have you.")[ And what does //this// critic (link-rerun: "say?")[(dialog: [That you're a liar. That your so-called art has been a fluke and a delusion. That your neoclassical tastes have already been long obsolete, and your attempts at modernizing efforts have left you a broken failure, sustaining on needless lies, lies told to those whom you think are inconsequential.], "You know, typical critic stuff.")] Ah, but you should block all of that out. The artist shouldn't care.
<br>(link-reveal: "The artist should only paint.")[(show:?hidden1)]
]]]]]
</ul>]<choices1|(hide:?choices1)


[]<show|
[
<br>
//"Here you go,"// Henri comes out from the kitchen, spilling tea as he strides over his clutter. //"Your favorite - Earl Gray. I stocked up on it before prices soared, so… Yeah, go ahead. What's mine's yours."//
<br>
You ask him (link-reveal: "if Jesse has been getting in the way.")[ What you mean, of course, is whether all of this stuff gave my poor baby a shock.
<br>
//"No, of course not! Don't you worry about it. I sort of confined her to my bedroom; she's in there right now. She's been on her best behavior. Really helpful, in fact."//
<br>
You blink at him, not knowing (link-reveal: "where to start.")[(show:?choices2)]
]]<hidden1|(hide:?hidden1)

[<ul>
<li>(link: "He's basically been imprisoning Jesse?")[(hide:?choices2)(replace:?blink)[
<br>You are about to ask him if he's basically been imprisoning Jesse, but then you remember that "imprisoning" was exactly what you've been doing to her all these years. So, you (link-reveal: "phrase it more gently")[, asking if she's been allowed out.
<br>//"Oh, don't you worry. There's plenty of space for her to jump around, but she doesn't do a lot of that. I've got the food, water, everything in there, too. She's very content, you'll see in a minute."//
<br>In a minute… It seems Henri has something else to say, so (link-reveal: "you let him.")[(show:?hidden2)]]]]

<li>(link: "She's… //helpful//?")[(hide:?choices2)(replace:?blink)[
<br>You almost chuckle at the thought. Jesse? Helpful? What, does she stand next to him with a light and a screwdriver, like he's fixing up a car? Like he's her dad? But you know (link-reveal: "what he meant")[ - she's helpful in the emotional sense. And Henri seems to need it. You ask him how his… work is going.
<br>//"That's right, oh I've been meaning to talk to you about it. Not work-work, per se, but, erm, it's about our neighbor, Mrs. Wong."//
<br>That's the last thing you want to hear about, but Henri seems tense, so you (link-reveal: "let him say what he has to say.")[(show:?hidden2)]]]]

<li>(link: "Can you just go meet your baby first?")[(hide:?choices2)(replace:?blink)[
<br>Impatient, you ask to see Jesse. Whatever question that you have, it'll be answered. It's not worth interrogating Henri over it. He (link-reveal: "doesn't seem all that well put-together")[, and that's saying a lot, coming from you.
<br>//"Yes, yes, of course, but she's sleeping anyway. Here, finish your tea first."//
<br>You tell him that you can always (link-reveal: "finish it later.")[
<br>//"Please, just a minute. I have something to tell you. It's about our neighbor - Mrs. Wong."//
<br>It's (link-reveal: "the last thing you want to hear.")[ But he grabs your arm. A bit too firm to be neighborly. A bit too much tremble. You're too frail, so you (link-reveal: "let him talk.")[(show:?hidden2)]]]]]]
</ul>]<choices2|(hide:?choices2)


[]<blink|
[
<br>
//"Yes… so, Mrs. Wong… (link-reveal: "I've found her")[(show:?hidden3)],"//` `[he says with a big grin, like a child waiting for claps and compliments.
<br>
