(set: $place to "at Henri's place")(replace: ?place)[$place]
(set: $activity to "a revelation")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

//"I actually did it, haha. I've found Mrs. Wong,"// Henri repeats excitedly, as if you didn't hear him the first time.
<br>
You manage to (link-reveal: "stammer out something")[:(show:?choices1)]

[<ul>
<li>(link: "Has he informed the police? Or the niece?")[(hide:?choices1)(replace: ?stammer)[Has he informed the police?
<br>//"No… no no, they're less than useless. They don't know what I know, and they don't care."//
<br>(link-reveal: "And the niece?")[
<br>//"Her? Why? Has she figured something out?"//
<br>(link-reveal: "What is he talking about?")[ How would you know?
<br>//"Oh… You mean for a funeral. Right."//
<br>She's (link-reveal: "dead")[ - you say - more of a statement than a question.
<br>//"I thought you knew."//
<br>You had (link-reveal: "a hunch.")[
<br>//"You've always had excellent intuition."//
<br>(link-reveal: "Where is this conversation going?")[
<br>//"Well, then you'd know that funerals and burials are where we lost a lot of data. Cremation, in-ground decomposition… What a waste! No-one thought to catalog the poses! There's still so much left to be done, and getting all sentimental now would be like erasing as we write. And I'm just collecting letters right now. But I'm onto something. They'll see. They'll all see."//
<br>This is getting exhausting. You make him (link-reveal: "say plainly what he knows.")[(show:?hidden1)]]]]]]
]]
<li>(link: "How did he find her? Did she just… appear?")[(hide:?choices1)(replace: ?stammer)[How did he find her?
<br>//"Heh, with a lot of leg work. A lot of late nights, too. The people at the precinct were not very helpful, imagine that. But I don't blame them. How would I even begin to explain to them?"//
<br>Explain what, that he knows the location of a missing person? (link-reveal: "Shouldn't they want to know that?")[
<br>//"They're beyond caring at this point. Half of them have got people in their own families missing as well. And everyday, some new quack comes out saying that they've heard the voice of God, and that they can divine the locations where someone's mom or dad would reappear. But I'm not like the rest of those people. I don't need everyone to believe me. The numbers speak for themselves."//
<br>You thumb your tea cup. So, Mrs. Wong… (link-reveal: "reappeared?")[
<br>//"Yes, quite typically, too. I was completely wrong about the state she would be in - the pose, I mean - but the spot was, well, spot-on, haha. I got lucky; many have been reappearing in different countries, not just counties. It was just about two hours' drive east of Riverpoint, off of some old hiking trails. I drove, and there she was, placed pretty high on a rock!"//
<br>Your head is swimming. You practically beg Henri to throw you a lifeline - he didn't actually answer your question - (link-reveal: "how did he figure all of this out?")[(show:?hidden1)]]]
]]
<li>(link: "Is she OK?")[(hide:?choices1)(replace: ?stammer)[There is a great hesitation between (link-reveal: "\"is she\" and \"OK\"")[, the latter sounds almost childish the moment it leaves your lips.
<br>//"Oh yes, Mrs. Wong was in excellent condition!"// Henri's eyes (link-reveal: "lights up.")[ //"Even though it was a hiking trail - not far from Riverpoint - there was no sign of post-mortem animal predation, meaning I got there just in time - MEANING, I was correct about the date. Too bad, I couldn't figure out the literal second of a reappearance, and I got her pose wrong, too, but there you go."//
<br>You don't know what to say. He keeps smiling that awkward smile of his like he expects you to be impressed. So… (link-reveal: "she's dead.")[
<br>//"Yeah…"// Henri says after thinking about it for a second.
<br>(link-reveal: "Is he not certain?")[
<br>//"Medically speaking, she's dead, sure. Some say they're still 'in there', but I don't buy it."//
<br>So he had (link-reveal: "her vitals measured?")[
<br>//"I didn't have the right equipment to test something like brain activity, but I felt no pulse. The body didn't relax after seventy-two hours either, so it wasn't regular rigor mortis. There's no reason to think that this was any different from all reported cases. Well, the only difference was… I found her."//
<br>He places the emphasis on "I" with a smile. It's a bait, a lure, and you'll bite: You ask him (link-reveal: "how he managed to figure out where Mrs. Wong was.")[(show:?hidden1)]]]]]]


]]
