[//"So I've been (link-reveal: "scraping")[_explain(dialog: [<i>"These machines here, they hear EVERYTHING. The admins told me that it couldn't be done, but what they mean is that they'll wait for me to do it at home, then they'll take all the credit."</i>],"There isn't a single radar dish in sight.")] for reports and feeding the numbers to (link-reveal: "the computer")[_explain(dialog: [<i>"They relocated the art department to make room for it. One day, that machine will make a file that's only a few gigabytes of everything there is to know."</i>],"The art department is a small price to pay.")] down in my university's basement. PLENTY to work with. There've been so many MORE disappearances, (link-reveal: "increasing")[_explain(dialog: [<i>"For three decades now, it was one case per year. Then, it was two per year. Then four per six-month period. Then eight…"</i>],"He goes on and on.")] by the day. You see, it follows a (link-reveal: "bifurcation pattern")[_explain(dialog: [<i>"It was so simple that it didn't even cross my mind!"</i>],"...")]. We've been in what's called the 'quiet zone', either the (link-reveal: "first or second")[_explain(dialog: [<i>"First? Or second? It really depends on which attractor is the correct one - I've got several hypotheses in mind, but I'm leaning towards this being the second period of stability."</i>],"He seems unstable.")]. Right now, things are regular enough for me to track down Mrs. Wong's location. But soon, it'll go back into (link-reveal: "chaos")[_explain(dialog: [<i>"Not randomness, mind you, but CHAOS, completely predetermined but unpredictable. Well, haha, it would be if I didn't have a powerful enough computer."</i>],"Does he 'have' it? Is it 'his'?")]. If I wait it out, the next 'quiet zone' will be in about (link-reveal: "a month")[_explain(dialog: [<i>"By then, there will be eight disappearances in a single day. Four will be in Brazil and Argentina, and the other four will spread around Iran, Syria, and…"</i>],"By then, you won't be around to hear him yammer, hopefully.")], and THEN, I'll be able to-"//
]<hidden1|(hide:?hidden1)

[
<br>
He stops when he sees your eyes (link-reveal: "glazing over.")[
<br>
//"Yeah. At least a part of my theory was correct."//
<br>
And (link-reveal: "what will he do with that theory of his?")[
<br>
//"Well, it never ends. Next, I'll have to figure out the exact timing, though I don't think whatever is causing this cares about clock-time. Something about the sun's angle, maybe?"//
<br>
(link-reveal: "What good is that?")[ Is that going to prevent future disappearances?
<br>
//"You- you're not getting the full picture,"// he says, scratching his chin. //"See, at this stage, we're just putting characters on a page - just where everything is. But next, we'll be able to read what the words are saying."//
<br>
Words? (link-reveal: "The people are words?")[
<br>
//"Yes, that's one way to put it. The mannequins, each with their own poses, are collectively saying something. Perhaps not exactly 'language' as you'd understand it, but with enough data points, a pattern will emerge. Only, I don't know where to begin. Maybe it'll come to me in a dream, just like how James Watson realized the double helix, ha!"//
<br>
He is smiling again. (link-reveal: "Isn't he afraid that he'll be next?")[
<br>
//"You know, if you do something enough, you'll stop worrying about where you're going. I think you said that in one of your talks."//
<br>
Henri, (link-reveal: "where is Mrs. Wong now?")[
<br>
//"Oh, she's in the back."//
<br>
You abruptly and very urgently remember that you're (link-reveal: "here for Jesse")[, and you need to (link-reveal: "stand up right now")[ and (link-reveal: "get her home as quickly as possible")[, since there are so many things you have left to do, namely (link-reveal: "locking your door tight.")[
<br>
//"Yes, sorry,"// Henri glances at his not-there watch. "//Where is my mind? Here, let me show you."//
<br>
