You're in a narrow hallway.
<br>
(link: "You take a step.")[The further you go, the harder it is to ignore the pungently sweet smell - like some disgustingly rich food for an otherwise non-human creature - that has been wafting in the air.
<br>
(link: "You take another step.")[The further you go, the less your feet want to carry on.
<br>
(link: "You take yet another step.")[The further you go, the more you feel him breathing on your back. Quickening. Giddy. Like a child's.
<br>
(link: "And another…")[The further you go, the stiffer you are.
<br>
(link: "And another.")[You arrive at a red door. Incongruously red. Swirling. You're dizzy from holding your breath, and you're beginning to see things. The brass handle is sticky in your hand.
<br>
(link-reveal: "You open the door.")[
<br>
//"Yeap, there she is!"// Henri bumps past you, like an enthusiastic curator going in before the crowd. (link-reveal: "//\"Aren't they getting along so well?\"//")[
