<!--heathy-->
[
<br>
Mrs. Wong stands naked with her back towards the door. Her hair is shaved clean. The bed beside her is full of photography equipment. You see a flicker of a tail from her arms. She is cradling Jesse, rocking arrhythmically (link-reveal: "once")[, then (link-reveal: "twice")[, then (link-reveal: "thrice")[, as if shaking Jesse awake.
<br>
Jesse! (link-reveal: "Get down from there!")[ You rush inside, hitting face-first that wall of stink, and another jab in your gut, the tea coming back up where it came in from.
<br>
//"Mraoow! Khhhh…"// startled, Jesse hisses at you from atop her morbid tree, bearing (link-reveal: "bloodied fangs.")[ She is already halfway through tearing Mrs. Wong's left cheek from her face, which now hangs a piece of wet jerky. Then, she realizes that it's just you, so she hops down from those cradling arms, kicking Mrs. Wong, and as she is about to topple, Henri (link-reveal: "catches her.")[ One moment later, you would have seen the corpse's face.
<br>
//"I've got it. No problem. No problem whatsoever. Oof, gotta watch what you're eating, Mrs. Wong."//
<br>
Jesse runs over to you and brushes her red whiskers against your leg. There, there, (link-reveal: "it's OK.")[ You hold her tight, trying to wipe her face with your fingers. You can't make it clean enough. The blood is on your hands now, and you cannot get it out. The iron stink has stained your sinus, and you will never be clean, ever, ever, ever. Your mouth feels sour. Jesse gazes at you with her huge eyes and licks the corners of her lips.
<br>
(link-reveal: "//\"Don't blame the poor thing; there's no harm done,\"//")[ Henri says as he props the corpse back up, examining the bleeding flesh. //"It's the overall shape that matters. As you can see, she's making a loop with her arms, but I expected it to be a 'three o'clock' pose - a perfectly perpendicular angle."//
<br>
Unable to contain it anymore, you scramble across the floor and (link-reveal: "hurl")[ in a bowl conveniently placed in the corner of the room. With bleary eyes, you recognize that it contains what would have been Jesse's kibble, now empty.
<br>
//"Oh my God, are you OK?"// Henri (link-reveal: "walks over")[, but you hold out a hand, making him stop. //"It's alright. I'll… I'll clean it after. Don't worry about it. Yeah, that's where I left food out for Jesse, but I must've forgotten to check. Sorry. Time flies when you're busy, right? Heh…"//
<br>
Then, the moment he turns away, perhaps to fetch Jesse's things, you (link-reveal: "hurry out of the red door")[, mumbling that it's time for Jesse's medication.
<br>
//"Oh, already? I haven't shown you…"// you hear Henri's voice calling from behind. //"I'll stop by yours to see those paintings of yours, alright? One of these days!"//
<br>
(link: "One of these days…")[
