You're back at home, looking high and low for Jesse, but she is nowhere to be found. Finally, you slump in one corner, head clamoring with thoughts, and you repeat over and over one question:
<br>
What do you do now?

(set: _numDead to 0)
(set: _doDead to "(set: _numDead to it + 1)(if: _numDead >= 3)[(show:?hiddenDead)]")

<br>
(link-reveal: "Call the neighbors?")[_doDead Yes, the neighbors. Who lives on this floor? The Perries are nice enough, but they'll never tell you where Jesse is. They secretly hate her for meowing and waking up their damnable kid. They secretly hate you. And then there's Mrs. Wong, who… Ah, you forget. You're not thinking straight. And what about the ones downstairs… You don't know anyone. They might not even be there anymore. You're all alone.]
<br>
(link-reveal: "Call the police?")[_doDead And what, you might as well call the fire brigade. But if you call the authorities, they'll swarm your place, where they will find what you've been doing in the dark? And hand it off to the Suppression Bureau? No, that's thinking too far. The police can't even find a missing woman, let alone a missing cat. You're better off dealing with this by yourself.]
<br>
(link-reveal: "Ask Henri for help?")[_doDead What's wrong with him? What's wrong with //you//? You've entrusted Jesse to that… man. Such a man. He didn't even recognize that something was amiss. Why would you think that his perceptual skill would be of any help? The man is as dull as a rock. You were a fool to think he'd be any different. He's only good at finding dead things. Speaking of, perhaps you ought to do something about your neighbor's… hobby. That's what you'd say if you were a busybody, and look how those end up. No, what's done is done. It's best that you look out for your best interest first - your peace.]

