The Gala happened (link-reveal: "yesterday.")[ You can imagine an army of diligent workers cleaning up whatever that's left in the Darkbloom Estate, and the curtains are drawn once again so that daylight won't damage the valuables. The promising and beautiful shake hands with the rich and powerful. In the morning, they pick up their tattered clothes from the hotel carpet. Something great has moved beneath the skin of the Earth. But since you weren't there, (link-reveal: "you can only imagine.")[
<br>
Now, you are idly surfing the (link-rerun: "internet")[(dialog: [An ocean of data, a desert of sense. It churns to the planet's collective cognition. The fishes are hopelessly ignorant of the storm.], "And so it goes.")]. Or rather, you float, face-up at the Sun, letting waves from the aether wash over you. Choke you. If you drown, no-one would know.

