[
<br>
Or rather, you don't quite understand (link-reveal: "what's playing out in front of you.")[
<br>
It appears to be a handheld footage, zooming into (link-reveal: "a person's face.")[ A very still, very blood-drained face. Now, it is not strange that clips of mannequins end up online; people's fascination outweighs federal proscription. But what confuses you more are glimpses of a very well-decorated hall, how crowded it is, and how many more of the unmoving figures there are, all standing on pedestals, each an inscrutable pose. Too evenly spaced. Too deliberately posed. The caption (link-reveal: "reads,")[
<br>
//"EXPOSED: The DISGUSTING DECADENCE of the AZTEC DEEP STATE and their CARNICERO CULTISTS. Can the TRAITORS and FASCISTS in Dallas deny involvement in this one? When will President Gore and his BOUGHT CRONIES grow some spine and PUSH THE BUTTON already?"//
<br>
(link: "Watch some more…")[Then, there are videos after videos of black-kevlar-ed soldiers, rifles at the ready, faces like some high-tech crustaceans, no identifying patch. (link-reveal: "Suppression.")[ Your breath seizes in your throat. They do not exist. But here they are, right on your screen, much to your terror. One of them appears immensely annoyed to be filmed by those whom one officer referred to as "stump-farming hicks" after the one filming failed to back off from the scene.
<br>
(link: "And some more…")[Elsewhere, in another video, a handful of the same "hicks" are lugging felling axes and hunting shotguns, following one of those armored men into an ornate door. Some confused screaming follows. A man yells,
<br>
//"Get your hands off me! Don't you know who I am?"//
<br>
But most only profess their ignorance, or they do not protest at all and instead await their lawyers. They are all very well-dressed almost as a rule. Some wear masks.
<br>
You watch and watch and refuse to believe your own eyes. It must be fake. Someone staged it. Or, (link-reveal: "you're imagining it.")[ The Darkbloom Foundation is as protected as an outfit can be within the Union. And yet, Suppression agents are there, raiding a Foundation-funded event. An event that you were supposed to be at. Just yesterday. Is there (link-reveal: "a putsch")[(dialog: [How would you know? You don't keep up with politics. You don't know who's who, and you've told yourself that you don't care, that it doesn't affect you.], "Nothing makes sense.")] going on? It doesn't matter - (link-reveal: "you weren't there.")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "But they will find a guest list")[, and your name is in there somewhere. Ah, a (link-reveal: "recidivist")[(dialog: [Once a zealot, always is. Insist on your innocence all you want, insist that you had no suspicion for the Foundation - they will find your name. You've already been let go once. They were simply waiting…], "... For you to mess up your second chance.").
<br>
You haven't been staying very quiet, (link-reveal: "have you?")[ You made a big splash, enough to attract the big fishes. Far bigger than you'd like to hope.
<br>
You close everything and gag and scream. The painting in the room's corner - you must (link-reveal: "destroy the accursed thing.")[ But as you crawl towards it, your stomach twists, and you gag again.
<br>
So you hurry into the bathroom and lean over the toilet bowl. Gag. Spit. Clear drool. You swallow and try to calm yourself, but breathing hurts. Your lungs are squeezing. (link-reveal: "This body is old and dying.")[ (link-reveal: "You torment it too much.")[ (link-reveal: "You'd best shed it soon.")[ Else, when they come for you, they will find you already trapped and bound. You (link-reveal: "flush.")[
<br>
The anxious thoughts have quieted somewhat. You lift up the veil and look at your unfinished painting.
<br>
It is too flawed. Too unremarkable. It is nothing. (link-reveal: "Not worth destroying")[; ironically, its destruction would only give it more value in mystique.
<br>
Anything you do now will seem suspicious. Your life since your first brush with them has been suspect. Perhaps… the best thing you can do now is to (link-reveal: "do nothing at all.")[ To breathe so slowly that you appear dead. To mind so little that you pass through the aether invisibly. The Sisters in the Winnipeg chapter showed you, (link-reveal: "didn't they?")[
<br>
Too bad, you were and have always been a poor student and a heartache to anyone who'd want to teach you anything. Else, you wouldn't be in this mess. Just thank Fortuna that you didn't go to that Gala, that you've thrown away your future prematurely.
<br>
It was all rotten anyway. Sweet, sweet rot.
<br>
---
