:: Jesse-Window A {"position":"5300,3900","size":"100,100"}
{=

(set: $activity to "contemplating the window")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

<!--lonely route, window open, Julia appears and talks to you-->
(set: $lockJesseWindowA to true)

The window is open, and (link-reveal: "a strange wind is blowing in.")[
<br>
How long has this window stayed closed? Since you took (link-rerun: "Jesse")[(dialog: [Cats fall to their deaths all the time, all for the crime of curiosity, of wanting to know another air.],"So the window stays shut.")] from the streets? Or even (link-rerun: "before that")[(dialog: [Seattle used to be more breathable, but the Union had to replace the factories and data centers that were lost to the secession. That was before you were even born.], "So the window stays shut.")]? The hinges have all rusted, and the glass has taken on a milky opaqueness.
<br>
(link-reveal: "This isn't so bad.")[ Sure, it smells like sulfur and smoke, but does that beat the smell of sweat and turpentine? Does staying here beat being out there? If to stay means to suffer the hell you've known, will you, as though the building is on fire, (link-reveal: "jump?")[
<br>
It is a four, five-story drop from here, depending on whether you will land on the second-floor yard or the parking lot. You will not land on your feet, for your head is heavy, and all of your nimbleness is in your fingers, not your limbs.
<br>
But the wind will blow in your face. Freedom. (link-reveal: "Glory.")[ For one moment, you will soar. Will you holler and scream? Or will the breath be taken from your lungs? Will the utter thrill of it blow you out like a candle seconds before you splash?
<br>
(link-reveal: "A choice")[ - that is all it takes to make living bearable. If there is any consolation, no matter how much you've squandered here, no matter how rotten you've become, there is always an "outside".
<br>
If you don't like it here, you can always leave, (link-reveal: "right Jesse?")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "Silence.")[
<br>
That's right, it's late already, and Jesse is sleeping. Somewhere. The thought that she has already left hasn't even crossed your mind.
<br>
When you go to sleep tonight, you will once again throw a dice and hope that Jesse still hasn't left when morning comes. Better you the gambler than Jesse. Being with you is becoming a (link-reveal: "greater and greater risk.")[
<br>
---
//(link: "\"Why don't you just get rid of it?\"")[(goto: "Jesse-Window A1")]//

<!--[[Jesse-Window A1]]-->

]]]]]]]]


:: Police D1 {"position":"4800,3850","size":"100,100"}
{=

(set: $activity to "𝑎̥̊⃝𝑤̥̊⃝𝑎̥̊⃝𝑘̥̊⃝𝑒̥̊⃝𝑛̥̊⃝")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

(link-reveal: "Quiver.")[ (link-reveal: "Shiver.")[ (link-reveal: "Shake.")[ (link: "Strength…")[Strength drains from your body, and (link: "youth…")[youth pours through your finger tips.
<br>
Starlight illuminates the linen above you. Shadows flutter and dance across it - the (link-reveal: "tent flap")[, the (link-reveal: "fronds of palms")[, the (link-reveal: "head of a horned goat")[, (link-reveal: "hands.")[
<br>
The tent (link-reveal: "opens.")[
<br>
Dark men filter into the tiny space, looming over you. Their red eyes swirl on their faces, like probes, like antennas. They've caught you naked, but you are wholly unsurprised. You try to (link-reveal: "bury your face into your pillow and cover yourself with your blanket")[ - angels, burrowers in Godmeat, grant rest today; their tomorrow will come.
<br>
But they are (link-reveal: "laying their metal on you.")[ Cold and hard metal. You do not resist, for it is what they do. And seeing your passivity, they lay their hands on you. Once again, you do not resist, for it is what happens at night.
<br>
(link-reveal: "//\"Get up.\"//")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "You do.")[ They bind your wrists together behind your back and throw a bag over your head and lead you barefoot and naked into the sand, their metal still pressed firmly against your back.
<br>
What about your horse, (link-reveal: "your prized mare?")[ Was it seized? Or set free? Either way, it was never yours to begin with.
<br>
After some distance and a few dunes, one of them (link-reveal: "speaks")[, sounding like mandibles clicking together, and another, somewhere far away, growls back.
<br>
Soon, you are set upon by (link-reveal: "a great zephyr")[, which stirs up a vortex, sand shredding against your skin, flying into your mouth, your nose… You hear the terrible sounds of terrible wings of a terrible (link-reveal: "chariot")[ as it descends on you and your captors. And though you cannot see it fully, you perceive its moving immensity through the linen veil.
<br>
They (link-reveal: "push their metal into your spine.")[ You shuffle forward and step onto the chariot and feel the soles of your feet grow cold. The monstrous swans, which drive such chariots, let out a dizzying screech, and their wings begin flapping again. Your knees grow weak as you are (link-reveal: "lifted from the Earth.")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "//\"What was all that for?\"//")[ One of them yells to another over the roaring gust. //"What was the point?"//
<br>
(link: "The second answer…")[//"Beats me,"// answers the second.
<br>
(link: "A third adds…")[//"Don't let the brass hear it,"// a third adds.
<br>
(link: "And the first retorts…")[//"What brass? They're all dead."//
<br>
(link: "And the third goes…")[//"Shush!"//
<br>
The high air blows cruelly, and you've become very, very still, growing (link-reveal: "colder and colder.")[ And through the black threads of the bag, (link-reveal: "you see…")[a glimmer. (link-reveal: "A vision of beauty")[, so far away, (link-reveal: "red")[ upon the horizon, like a (link-reveal: "burning 𝑤̥̊⃝𝑜̥̊⃝𝑢̥̊⃝𝑛̥̊⃝𝑑̥̊⃝.")[
<br>
---
(align:"=><=")+(box:"X")[<h2>(link: "The Sun has come at last.")[(goto: "Police D2")]</h2>]<!--[[Police D2]]-->

]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]


:: Police D2 {"position":"4800,3975","size":"100,100"}
{=
(replace: ?date)[??]
(set: $time to "Dream")(replace: ?time)[$time]
(set: $place to "nowhere")(replace: ?place)[$place]
(set: $activity to "being questioned")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

(set: $lockPoliceD to true)

Before you is a metal table, lit by a single lamp. Your entire body is hurting.
<br>
(link-reveal: "//\"Hello, friend,\"//")[ out of the dark comes a woman's voice. //"Didn’t think we’d meet again so soon."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "You ask where you are.")[
<br>
//"Nowhere."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "You ask what the point of doing this is.")[ You've told her a thousand times before, and you will tell her another thousand times - that you've done nothing wrong. You haven't done (link-rerun: "anything")[(dialog: [Not move, not talk, not breathe. Nothing.], "Like you've promised.")] at all.
<br>
//"Yes, yes, 'tending to your garden'. I know."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "Then why are you here?")[ You've been so good, so harmless, so out-of-the-way. You didn't know that the Darkbloom people were of interest to the Bureau. (link-reveal: "You even skipped the gala.")[
<br>
//"Well, I can't speak on behalf of the Bureau, but it's curious, isn't it - how you were in frequent contact with them for the weeks, months, even years leading up to their event. And suddenly, right before they were got… nothing."//
<br>
Like you said: (link-reveal: "Nothing.")[ There's no point anymore. You just want to stay home with Jesse and finish your pointless painting. You can't hurt anyone. She doesn't need to interrogate you anymore.
<br>
//"Interrogate? Is that what you think this is? I'm sorry, but you've misunderstood completely. This is a confessional. For you. Before the end."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "The end?")[ Is it time already?
<br>
//"Almost, but yes."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "Finally.")[
<br>
//"Oh don't be too hasty. There's always next time. Tomorrow always comes."//
<br>
Tomorrow, then the day after, and the day after that. All days are the same. (link-reveal: "There's no point.")[
<br>
//"There you go again with that talk. It's so tiring. Come on, I think we both deserve a little more fanfare. The Sun's out; it's a beautiful day."//
<br>
You gaze around at (link-reveal: "the pitch blackness surrounding you")[, then you turn back towards where the voice is coming from and tell her that no matter how long she keeps you here, (link-reveal: "you'll always give the same answer.")[
<br>
---
(link: "//\"Great, then you won't mind doing it one more time, right?\"//")[(goto: "Police D3")]<!--[[Police D3]]-->
]]]]]]]]]]]


:: Police D3 {"position":"4800,4100","size":"100,100"}
{=

(replace: ?date)[??]
(set: $time to "Dream")(replace: ?time)[$time]
(set: $place to "nowhere")(replace: ?place)[$place]
(set: $activity to "being questioned")(replace: ?activity)[$activity]

(set: $lockPoliceD to true)


<!--Henri branch-->
(if: $choiceJesseGala is "Henri")[//"What is your relationship with Henri Roy-Boudreau?"//

[<ul>
<li>(link: "He's a neighbor.")[(hide:?Henri1)(show:?hiddenHenri1)(replace:?responseHenri1)[You say that Henri is a neighbor. Nothing more.]]
<li>(link: "He's a friend.")[(hide:?Henri1)(show:?hiddenHenri1)(replace:?responseHenri1)[You say that Henri is a friend. A decent one, up to a point.
<br>//"And you said you were staying perfectly put."//
<br>She's been calling you "friend", but that doesn't make you buddies. You don't entertain her jab.]]
<li>(link: "You don't know him, not really.")[(hide:?Henri1)(show:?hiddenHenri1)(replace:?responseHenri1)[You say that you're only superficial acquaintances. Anymore than that, you can't comment.]]
</ul>]<Henri1|

[
<br>
[]<responseHenri1|
<br>
//"Oh? So tight-lipped all of a sudden. You were going on and on about his various 'theories' and 'investigations'. Said he was onto something big."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "That wasn't what you said.")[ That was what he said of himself. He's always like that. You thought you understood, but you didn't, and you didn't care enough to find out. (link-reveal: "Better to not speak of the unspeakable.")[
<br>
//"Right… There was a dead body - one Mrs. Caroline Wong - inside his home, which you frequent. (link-reveal: "Would you comment on it?")[(show:?Henri2)]"//
]]]<hiddenHenri1|(hide:?hiddenHenri1)

[<ul>
<li>(link: "No.")[(hide:?Henri2)(show:?hiddenHenri2)(replace:?responseHenri2)[No - you say. She and you have been over this before. It doesn't lead anywhere. She's not interested in finding out the culprit, as if she already knew.]]
<li>(link: "He didn't kill anyone.")[(hide:?Henri2)(show:?hiddenHenri2)(replace:?responseHenri2)[He didn't kill anyone - you say. But you know she's not interested in prosecuting murders. The kinds of crime she deals in is far greater. The crime of //being//, for example.]]
<li>(link: "You had nothing to do with it.")[(hide:?Henri2)(show:?hiddenHenri2)(replace:?responseHenri2)[You had nothing to do with it - you say. You were in shock. You couldn't think properly before her people showed up. It was as though they've laid a trap for you.]]
</ul>]<Henri2|(hide:?Henri2)

[
<br>
[]<responseHenri2|
<br>
//"Tsk, we all would like to say that… Well, like you said, it doesn't matter anymore."//
<br>
You grow impatient with her: (link-reveal: "What's next?")[ Ask you about the computer in his university basement? About what he did with it? Might as well ask you what your solution to the secession conflict is. Surely, if Henri and his gizmos of any threat, (link-reveal: "she and her Bureau would know better than you do.")[(show:?common)]

]]<hiddenHenri2|(hide:?hiddenHenri2)
]


<!--Amy branch-->
(else-if: $choiceJesseGala is "Amy")[//"What is your relationship with Amy Wong?"//

[<ul>
<li>(link: "She's Mrs. Wong's niece.")[(hide:?Amy1)(show:?hiddenAmy1)(replace:?responseAmy1)[She's the bereaved niece of the neighborhood missing woman - you say, matter-of-factly. The woman stays silent, not convinced. It's not so strange that Amy comes around often. What's stranger is why you've been questioned about it. What does the Bureau want with her?]]
<li>(link: "She's someone in need.")[(hide:?Amy1)(show:?hiddenAmy1)(replace:?responseAmy1)[She was in need, and you were there to help her.
<br>//"And here I thought you've been staying put."//
<br>What were you supposed to do? She was beside herself. She seemed so lonely. You took her in like you took Jesse in. When she was doing better, she left you. They all do. Tale as old as time. Nothing of interest to the Bureau.]]
<li>(link: "She's someone special.")[(hide:?Amy1)(show:?hiddenAmy1)(replace:?responseAmy1)[Amy is… Sun-spark, starlight to those with the eyes to see, moonshine for those thirsting for joy. But how would you explain matters of aesthetics to blind philistines? You don't, of course. You are lucky if this woman thinks little of art.
<br>So, you tell her that Amy is just a girl, one among a billion, and the Bureau should want nothing from her.]]
</ul>]<Amy1|

[
<br>
[]<responseAmy1|
<br>
//"Like I said, I can't speak on the Bureau's behalf."//
<br>
Then (link-reveal: "why does she want to know about Amy?")[
<br>
//"Because you've spent a lot of time with her leading up to… well. It might be significant. It might not. Just tell me (link-reveal: "what you've been doing with her these past few weeks.")[(show:?Amy2)]"//
]]<hiddenAmy1|(hide:?hiddenAmy1)

[<ul>
<li>(link: "You've been teaching her.")[(hide:?Amy2)(show:?hiddenAmy2)(replace:?responseAmy2)[You've been teaching her, preparing her. What do you teach her? To explore her own potential. What do you prepare her for? For the future, of course. And when the future is dark, one needs keen eyes and a youthful, capable body.
<br>You only tell the woman that you've been teaching Amy how to paint.]]
<li>(link: "You've been enjoying her company.")[(hide:?Amy2)(show:?hiddenAmy2)(replace:?responseAmy2)[You've been basking in her light, like a sunbathing cat, and when she leaves, you are all warm and glowing with youthful vigor. It is not that you are healthier - this body is wilting away, and your skin hangs like rags upon a dead branch - but rather, you acquire that essential lack that all youths possess: Want. You want, more than ever, to live.
<br>You tell the woman that you and Amy have been chatting about whatever inconsequential thing Amy wanted.]]
<li>(link: "You've been killing time.")[(hide:?Amy2)(show:?hiddenAmy2)(replace:?responseAmy2)[You've been biding your time. Waiting. They say it is calmest before a storm, and you sometimes wish that you can go on forever, to have endless afternoons with wine and wake up the next day with a heavy head and a light heart. But you've done plenty of that. You are too old for simple joys. You cannot wait but must.
<br>You tell the woman "nothing", and she chuckles.]]
</ul>]<Amy2|(hide:?Amy2)

[
<br>
[]<responseAmy2|
<br>
//"Same old, huh? No matter how much things change, old habits die hard."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "You get impatient with her")[: What business does she or the Bureau, for that matter, have with what you do in private or whom you associate with? Amy is an adult and can decide for herself how she dispenses with her time and energy.
<br>
//"Spoken like you can't do anything about it."//
<br>
Yes, that's right. You can't help it. What matters is that everyday, Amy leaves the apartment (link-reveal: "whole and well.")[
<br>
//"And somehow, you grow fuller."//
<br>
Full? (link-reveal: "Everyday, you grow hungrier.")[ Everyday, there is less of you. Would this woman prefer it if you withered completely? Is that why you're kept here? Is that what the Bureau is for? While the world they protect is languishing, (link-reveal: "they choose to waste their time and resources to torment you.")[(show:?common)]
]]]]<hiddenAmy2|(hide:?hiddenAmy2)

]

<!--Lonely branch-->
(else-if: $choiceJesseGala is "window")[//"You've been leading a lonely life."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "Is that a question?")[
<br>
//"Everything is a question if you listen closely."//

[<ul>
<li>(link: "She's asking //why// you're so alone.")[(show:?hiddenlonely1)(hide:?lonely1)(replace:?responselonely1)[//Why// are you alone? For it is a mark of virtue and innocence; your isolation disqualifies you from suspicion, whatever she and her people may have of you. For you've promised to stay put - the freedom to crawl in exchange for clipped wings.
<br>But truly? Perhaps out of habit, though that wasn't always the case. Perhaps you felt tired on the same day that the world came knocking, though you were alive and awake on the day when the world slept. Perhaps it was sheer chance, and you fell through the cracks. 
<br>And in those cracks, you 've been crawling, while others were crushed beneath the soles of giants.]]
<li>(link: "She's asking if you've made any friend.")[(show:?hiddenlonely1)(hide:?lonely1)(replace:?responselonely1)[Have you made //any// friend? Or rather, have you met anyone who you didn't try to extract something out of, even if it is only their life force?
<br>You knew that it was against your nature to turn others away. You've always been hungry for others, yearning to reach out, and to touch. But you knew too how dangerous a starving and desperate lioness stalking her trash-filled cage is. You saw what you could do.
<br>So, you made a promise to yourself: To only chase that which you are wholly incapable of grasping, of sinking your teeth into, of ruining, even if it, in turn, destroys you.]]
<li>(link: "She's asking if this approach truly was the best.")[(show:?hiddenlonely1)(hide:?lonely1)(replace:?responselonely1)[Was this //truly// the best you could do? Is this your happy ending?
<br>You've done everything right. You've worked with diligence, and against your own nature, you've turned away that which others work for - a chance at living. The world extended a hand, and you, as promised, turned away.
<br>You are reminded of the story of Lot's wife, who gazed back at her fallen past and was immediately turned into a Galatean pillar of salt, stricken by the perfect light which has started it all. You only look forward and carry on, even if you hobble, crutchless.]]
</ul>]<lonely1|
]

[
<br>
[]<responselonely1|
<br>
//"You're quiet all of a sudden."//
<br>
(link-reveal: "Is that another question?")[
<br>
//"Alright, why did you go quiet?"//
<br>
(link-reveal: "You got caught up in your own thoughts, that's all.")[
<br>
//"Be careful. Even if you keep to yourself, some thoughts are loud. Too loud. It attracts the wrong kind of attention."//
<br>
What is she, (link-reveal: "the thought police?")[ Paranoia is her curse. The Bureau's curse. It is an institution founded in secrecy, to find things too terrible to exist, to guard against that which, if found, means that it's already too late. (link-reveal: "A pointless organization.")[ (link-reveal: "A pointless person.")[(show:?common)]
]]]]]<hiddenlonely1|(hide:?hiddenlonely1)

