<!--None branch-->
(else-if: $choiceJesseGala is "none")[//"You're struggling."//
<br>
Yes, (link-reveal: "what kind of a question is that?")[
<br>
//"It's not a question. Just an observation."//
<br>
Based on (link-reveal: "what")[, the fact that you've been confined to a dark cell, not knowing how many days has passed, not knowing if your cat lives or dies?
<br>
//"Your cat…"// she pauses, as if to look at you, though you cannot see her. //"Like I said, you've been struggling. (link-reveal: "Things weren't so bad when we first met all those years ago.")[(show:?none1)]"//
]]

[<ul>
<li>(link: "You were young and promising.")[(show:?hiddennone1)(hide:?none1)(replace:?responsenone1)[Things were different because you were different. You were young - perhaps a few wrinkles had appeared, but there was hope.
<br>In the ensuing years, you've aged decades. All those promises weighed heavily. They hollowed you out from within and blotted out the Sun from your eyes.
<br>Sobriety - it was supposed to be good for you, what a woman of health and sound mind ought to have. You're not just thinking about drinks either, though that was certainly part of your vitality.
<br>You thought that you'd live forever, that if you had squandered anything, there would always be more to take from the world. The Sun shines incessantly.]]
<li>(link: "You've lost so much.")[(show:?hiddennone1)(hide:?none1)(replace:?responsenone1)[You were somebody. Your greatest headache used to be choosing what or whom to turn down. You were esteemed.
<br>But above all, the act of creating used to be easy for you. "Easy" wasn't even the right word, since it was harder not to make things, do things, be things. You didn't strain to sit in one place. You didn't get heart palpations over the thought of getting out of bed, let alone picking up the brush. You were a "genius", as your father had put it.
<br>But your father is long dead. Your mother might as well be dead. Everyone you've ever known in that life is a distant memory. Even your token betrothed is gone. Everything could be dispensed with, else you'd never take flight.]]
<li>(link: "It's all her fault.")[(show:?hiddennone1)(hide:?none1)(replace:?responsenone1)[Yes, things changed when you met her. How far you have fallen. But a fall is never sudden. We only ignore the signs. Perhaps she, sitting there in the dark, has always been there. Watching. Waiting. Like the bacteria in your gut, she has waited for the signal - death - to consume you from within. All light casts a shadow; the brighter the light, the more horrible the dark.
<br>//"This is ridiculous,"// she says. //"Here I am, thinking I'm doing others a service, and I never get any thanks for it."//
<br>She insists that without her, you would have self-destructed more spectacularly. But wasn't it //her// who forced you to go see a shrink? Wasn't it her who kept you on the straight-and-narrow? It was so straight, so narrow, like the four walls of a cell. Or an apartment.]]
</ul>]<none1|(hide:?none1)

[
<br>
[]<responsenone1|
<br>
You hear a sigh.
<br>
(link-reveal: "//\"But it wasn't always this way.\"//")[
<br>
No, but one never knows what's going on behind the scenes. (link-reveal: "People change.")[
<br>
//"Yes, but you used to have (link-reveal: "someone")[(show:?none2)]. Someone who understood you, who knew exactly what you were."//
]]]<hiddennone1|(hide:?hiddennone1)

[<ul>
<li>(link: "You-know-who.")[(hide:?none2)(show:?hiddennone2)(replace:?responsenone2)[You-know-who - your once-betrothed, embarrassing to think. Embarrassing in the same way how one might shrivel up in disgrace whenever one thinks about themselves at something-teen, so convinced that their ephemera is what makes them, so insistent on the fact they've got it all figured out, so eager to fall into line.
<br>You thought, too, that you were understood. But did you not understand yourself, that you'd need a mirror? Or was this a disguise? Why hold yourself hostage while you can simply be yourself? This is you.]]
<li>(link: "You were too glad to be rid of him.")[(hide:?none2)(show:?hiddennone2)(replace:?responsenone2)[You-know-who. You've expunged his name from your memory because you didn't need it anymore. The moment he took off that ring, he became nothing. Everything he contained was gone, leaving only skin, like rags, like a trash bag, blowing in the wind.
<br>So, what does that make you, one who wears others like trash bags? You must have seemed insane. Better naked than insane.
<br>There was no denying what you were. You didn't need to be understood. You didn't need a mirror.]]
<li>(link: "It's all his fault.")[(hide:?none2)(show:?hiddennone2)(replace:?responsenone2)[You-know-who. He's the //real// reason why you're here. For years, he'd tell you that he understood you, that he was the only thing standing between you and… this.
<br>He accompanied you. He aided you. He told you that he wanted to see you become your best self. Of course, that was under the condition that he would be there, like a parasite, to have his time in the Sun as well.
<br>After Katherine, he changed his tune. He wanted the Sun for himself. You denied him. So, in Mexico City, he plunged you into darkness.]]
</ul>]<none2|(hide:?none2)

