It's already (link-reveal: "too late for the main events.")[ But you, hard-headed, willful, intend on scrounging whatever that's left. Opportunity does not wait for one with pride. So, (link-reveal: "you go.")[
<br>
The streets are (link-reveal: "quiet at this hour.")[ Except for some distant siren wails. Except for the howling wind, which picks up during your walk to the bus station, blowing the painting back. If you were any lighter, you’d take off with the gale. Actually flying would mean you'll make it to the gala in the nick of time instead of arriving the morning after. Still, you remain aground, and so you can only hope for a miracle.
<br>
(link-reveal: "You clutch the frames tight.")[ These are (link-rerun: "your wings")[(dialog: [Whereas fowls grow wings because they cannot help it, you've grown yours by your own will. There were too many times you could have given up. But you didn't.], "And that's why they're yours.")] of linen, coated in oil; they will take you far. (link-reveal: "The world will see.")[
<br>
You are (link-reveal: "right on time for your ride.")[ You buy two tickets, not trusting the luggage compartment with your //magnum opus//. Most of the seats are empty; few go where you’re heading. As you’re settling down, the old speakers crackle with some pre-recorded message - first in English, then in Spanish - neither of which you can make out a single word, not even the destination’s name. If you boarded the wrong bus, you wouldn’t even know.
<br>
(link-reveal: "You wait")[, and (link-reveal: "wait")[, and (link-reveal: "wait")[, but the bus is still parked. The driver drums on the wheel with his finger and glances at his watch. (link-reveal: "What is everyone waiting for?")[ Each passing minute is a minute you're later, and the horizon of your future closes inch by inch. By the time you arrive, everyone who matters will have left, and it would have been all in vain. Impatient, you (link-reveal: "pick at your lips")[ and (link-reveal: "your cuticles")[ and (link-reveal: "all the skin that is loose")[, shedding and lightening yourself so that the bus ride may (link-reveal: "quicken.")[
<br>
(link-reveal: "Hiss.")[ The door finally folds shut. The suspension creaks alive. You jerk backward - the vehicle has (link-reveal: "begun to move.")[ You breathe out and try to get some shut-eye.
<br>

[
