(either:
"(link-reveal: \"The machines - what are they for?\")[ The only thing you recognize is your laptop. Else, the work table resembles the dashboard of some decrepit starship. Cables disappear into piles of moldy takeouts and rotting newspapers. The apartment seems like a terminally ill patient, hooked up to things one hopes to never see in one's life.(show:?hidden1)]",
"(link-reveal: \"A man has been here.\")[ Even before noticing the man-clothes and the man-things, you've already felt it - a constriction of the breath. A shortening of the self. It is an old feeling. You thought you were free.(show:?hidden1)]",
"(link-reveal: \"Someone has been taking care of you.\")[ Keeping you alive, drip-feeding a terminal body so that it'd still wake up and shamble around and keep on working.(show:?hidden1)]",
)

[
<br>
(link-reveal: "Henri.")[ (either:
"Why is //he// here? Worse still, have //you// invited him in? Were you feeling lonely? Hungry? Did he promise you sweet things? Delicious things?(show:?hidden2)",
"Who else? Every time you look away, a man moves in, and with him comes all of his things. Maybe it's the only reason you haven't starved yet. But if that's the case, maybe you should have just starved.(if: $storyAnts's healthy is true)[ Then again, there's Jesse to think about.](show:?hidden2)",
"Doesn't he have a place of his own, a place that's two, three times the size of this hole? Why is he //here//? Simple. It's because //you// have nowhere else to go.(show:?hidden2)",
)]
]<hidden1|(hide:?hidden1)

[
<br>
(link-reveal: "You wrack your brain, trying to remember how it happened.")[ (either:
"Henri has always been here, somewhere out of view. Then, one day, he mustered up the courage to ask you out. There was a party. Did you go? What happened afterward? //This//. This happened.(show:?hidden3)",
"There was a party. And there was tea, a heady amount of it. And there were conversations. And… and… Was that all it took?(show:?hidden3)",
"You feel nauseous, as if you've hit your head. You aren't the sentimental sort, are you? You don't like to remember these things. Accept it. He's always been here.(show:?hidden3)",
)]
]<hidden2|(hide:?hidden2)

[
<br>
He's been here while your 𝑚̥̊⃝𝑎̥̊⃝𝑔̥̊⃝𝑛̥̊⃝𝑢̥̊⃝𝑚̥̊⃝ 𝑜̥̊⃝𝑝̥̊⃝𝑢̥̊⃝𝑠̥̊⃝ was out in the open, naked, exposed, wantonly displayed for his viewing pleasure.
<br>
(link-reveal: "Maybe it's meant to be.")[ You shouldn't be surprised. You already know what to do: Just live. Move on with your life. You will have forgotten about all of this tomorrow. Just focus on doing what you were always going to do anyway. He's not here //now//, (link-reveal: "is he?")[ 
